data.content:
Here's what breaks in EF Core 10 and how to fix each piece:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — expression tree no longer compiles

**What changed:** `ExecuteUpdateAsync` now accepts a regular `Func<>` instead of `Expression<Func<>>`. Your manual expression-tree code won't compile.

**Fix — dramatically simpler:**

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more `Expression.Lambda`/`Expression.Call` needed.

---

## 2. Complex type column names — two breaking changes

**a) Duplicate names are now uniquified** (e.g. `Street` becomes `Street1` for the second one).  
**b) Nested complex types use the full path** (`Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` → column `Payment_BillingAddress_City` instead of just `BillingAddress_City`).

**Fix — pin explicit column names to preserve your existing schema:**

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street"));
});

// Nested: pin the old column name
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City"); // old name without full path
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

**What changed:** All methods (`CommandReaderExecuting`, `CommandReaderExecuted`, etc.) gained a `string logCommandText` parameter for redacted SQL logging.

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)   // ← add this parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText for logging (constants redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual SQL
    }
}
```

Update all method overrides on the interface similarly.
